Route normal OSC 52 writes to the default clipboard so browser clients receive
terminal copy requests. Explicit clipboard types use an in-memory map in
BrowserClipboardService, so sending the normal 'c' destination as 'clipboard'
never reaches navigator.clipboard.writeText. Keep PRIMARY selection and reads
unchanged.

Reproduce in a browser terminal by running:
  printf '\033]52;c;Q0xJUEJPQVJEX1RFU1Q=\007'
Pasting into another application should yield CLIPBOARD_TEST. Without the fix,
the browser clipboard retains its previous value. Covered end-to-end in
 test/e2e/terminal.test.ts, with destination mapping cases in the VS Code patch.

Index: code-server/lib/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminal/browser/xterm/xtermTerminal.ts
===================================================================
--- code-server.orig/lib/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminal/browser/xterm/xtermTerminal.ts
+++ code-server/lib/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminal/browser/xterm/xtermTerminal.ts
@@ -343,7 +343,8 @@ export class XtermTerminal extends Disposable implements IXtermTerminal, IDetach
 					return _clipboardService.readText(type === 'p' ? 'selection' : 'clipboard');
 				},
 				async writeText(type: string, text: string): Promise<void> {
-					return _clipboardService.writeText(text, type === 'p' ? 'selection' : 'clipboard');
+					// Explicit clipboard types are in-memory only in the browser.
+					return _clipboardService.writeText(text, type === 'p' ? 'selection' : undefined);
 				}
 			});
 			this.raw.loadAddon(this._clipboardAddon);
